      "id": 1,
      "text": "New Post was established after the original village of Post was flooded by the construction of the Winter dam in 1922.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Post%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Thaddeus Thayer started a trading post in the area around 1865 and married an Ojibwe woman named Mary Anibish.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Post%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the late 1800s, the trading post at New Post served as the north terminus of the Chippewa Trail tote road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Post%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ignatius church was built in New Post to replace St. Anthony church, which was left on an island after flooding.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Post%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community of New Post is located on the south shore of the Chippewa Flowage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Post%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Ojibwe community of Pahquawong once lay along the west fork of the Chippewa River near New Post.",
